<h3>YouTube Audio Library — My Go-To Free Source</h3>
<p>Access it at <code>studio.youtube.com → Audio Library</code>. It's built into YouTube Studio, so you know every track is cleared for YouTube monetization. The quality is decent — not cinematic, but perfectly usable for talking-head videos, tutorials, and vlogs. Filter by mood, genre, and duration.</p>

<p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Download tracks at 320kbps (highest quality available). Use the "Attribution not required" filter to avoid crediting hassles. The emotional/ambient tracks are surprisingly good for B-roll sequences.</p>

<h3>Pixabay Music</h3>
<p>Same platform as the stock footage site. Quality varies wildly — some tracks are professional, others sound like a student's first GarageBand project. Worth browsing if you need something specific (Indian classical fusion, lo-fi beats) that YouTube Audio Library doesn't have.</p>

